# ============================================================
# FILES EXCLUDED FROM THE VERCEL DEPLOYMENT UPLOAD
# ============================================================
# .gitignore does not govern what Vercel uploads. It uploads the
# working directory, so anything present locally is uploaded unless
# it is excluded here or already ignored by the platform.
#
# Two rules govern this file:
#   1. Never exclude anything the deployed application reads.
#   2. Never exclude a secret.
#
# WHAT THE DEPLOYED APPLICATION MUST RECEIVE
#   api/index.py, app/, index.html, store.db, requirements.txt,
#   pyproject.toml, uv.lock, .python-version, vercel.json,
#   main.py, database.py. Nothing below matches any of those.
# ============================================================

# --- SECRETS: never upload, never ship ---
.env
.env.*

# --- LOCAL TOOLING ---
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.gitignore

# --- VERCEL LINK METADATA (per-machine, regenerated by `vercel link`) ---
.vercel/

# --- RUNTIME STATE: written at runtime under /tmp on Vercel ---
# These are local leftovers. Uploading them would ship stale
# sessions, approvals and uploads that the deployment cannot use.
app_meta.db
app_meta.db-journal
app_meta.db-wal
app_meta.db-shm
uploads/

# --- UNTRACKED WORK-IN-PROGRESS AND DEMO MATERIAL ---
# Not part of this application. Every one of these is untracked, so
# nothing that ships depends on it.
*_demo/
agent_chat_ui_demo/
context_state_demo/
dynamic_agents_demo/
email_assistant_demo/
human_in_the_loop_demo/
managing_long_conversations_demo/
mcp_demo_2/
multi_agent_demo/
wedding_planner_demo/
request.json
stitch-reference.png

# --- TESTS ---
# The deployment runs the application, not the suite, and pytest is
# not installed in the production environment. Excluded to keep the
# uploaded function small.
tests/

# --- DOCUMENTATION AND LOCKFILE NOT NEEDED AT RUNTIME ---
# requirements.txt is the pinned, generated install list the build
# actually uses; uv.lock is its source and is kept in git for
# reproducibility rather than uploaded.
uv.lock